==Personality==
{{Quote|You think I don't know? When it's hero time, if I mess up, somebody could die. From what you told me, if we mess up this time, everybody could die... Maybe that's too much to have in your head when you have to win. Maybe if I pretend everything is a big joke, when the time comes, I'll be able to do what I have to do.|10-year-old Ben to 17-year-old [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]] asking him to be serious.<ref name="TFoC"/>}}
Initially cocky, childish, and selfish, Ben's immaturity and attention-seeking behavior often led him to joke around, regardless of the situation, which landed him in trouble with adults. When he was 10 years old, he often used the [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]] improperly in order to benefit himself instead of actually helping others, such as using [[Grey Matter (Classic)|Grey Matter]] to search cereal boxes for a gold '''[[Sumo Slammers (Classic)|Sumo Slammer]]''' card.<ref name="WBC">''[[Washington B.C.]]''</ref> His allies often criticized his attitude, unaware of the fact that he used humor to mask his fears.<ref name="TFoC">''[[The Forge of Creation]]''</ref> It was also implied that, on some level, Ben helped people to get rewards<ref name="WBC" /> and for the thrill of being a hero, rather than because it was the right thing to do.<ref>[[Tetrax Shard (Classic)|Tetrax Shard]]</ref><ref name="SOTO" /> Despite some childish attitude, Ben was heroic, caring and generally good-natured, always willing to save others at any time even at the risk of himself. In spite of this good nature, heroism, and his moments of maturity, Ben could occasionally get carried away when it came to fame and recognition.<ref name="LG">''[[Lucky Girl (Episode)|Lucky Girl]]''</ref> This led him to act rather arrogantly and recklessly, and occasionally made dire mistakes and alienated his loved ones. However, he was quick to realize his mistakes and is quick to take responsibility and knew not to take things too far.<ref name="K11" />

Over the years, Ben has displayed good leadership skills, as well as the ability to adapt his attitude to a situation, becoming serious when it's called for. He became more mature, responsible and sensible. He continues to be kind-hearted and willing to lay down his own life for others, such as when he attempted to sacrifice himself to set the sentient [[Ultimate Forms]] free from the [[Ultimatrix (Original)|Ultimatrix]].<ref name="TUS">''[[The Ultimate Sacrifice]]''</ref> His idealistic views and unwillingness to compromise his values – aspects condemned by [[Azmuth (Classic)|Azmuth]],<ref name="WotW1">''[[War of the Worlds: Part 1]]''</ref> yet commended by others – sometimes drive him to act against reason, such as helping his enemies if they need it (most remarkably [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]]).<ref>''[[Ghost Town]]''</ref> [[Professor Paradox]] has praised Ben's good nature, going so far as to say he had the gift to make the right choices at the right moments, and even Azmuth himself states that Ben ultimately always does the right thing.<ref name="TFoC" /> Also, Ben doesn't give up and wouldn't let anyone stop him from doing what's right for those in need, especially his family, friends and mentors, or to bring enemies down, even when he once got a broken arm.<ref name="CaFS" /> 

However, even as a teen, Ben still displays some of his negative childish traits at times, which usually comes to light when Ben gets too caught up with fame much to the annoyance of [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]] and Kevin.<ref name="EotB">''[[Eye of the Beholder]]''</ref> Ben also has a violent, aggressive side: when Ben fails to save someone, is worried about the well-being his loved ones, or if people get hurt because of his failure, he becomes angry and lashes out, even at people he cares about. Perhaps the most notable of these instances is when Kevin willingly [[Ultimate Kevin|mutated]] himself to stop [[Aggregor]], Ben was determined to kill Kevin, even fighting Gwen when she refused to help him. During the episode, Ben confessed to [[Max Tennyson (Classic)|Max]] that he felt guilty for letting fame get into his head and claimed that he was trying to act more mature for once.<ref name="AP1">''[[Absolute Power: Part 1]]''</ref> He also threatened to hunt down and destroy the [[Forever Knights]] if [[Sir Driscoll|Driscoll]] did not promise to cease hunting down aliens.<ref name="The Purge" />

Ben has experienced trust issues, when it comes to automatically trusting everybody and teaming up with people whose true colors are later revealed and turns against [[Ben's Team|the team]].<ref name="ATG">''[[All That Glitters]]''</ref><ref name="BOAF"> ''[[Birds of a Feather]]''</ref> 

Though often perceived as unintelligent because of his immaturity and constant joking, Ben is cunning and resourceful when needed, quickly adapting when the Omnitrix doesn't provide him with the alien he wanted. He has once admitted that people assume he's not paying attention, but he actually is.<ref name="BT" />

In '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]''', Ben started thinking of himself as more of a superhero than a [[Plumbers (Classic)|Plumber]], often remarking that he's not a cop, but a superhero.<ref name="TMTC2">''[[The More Things Change: Part 2]]''</ref>

