==Etymology==
Benjamin is a name from the Hebrew name בִּנְיָמִין (Binyamin) which means "son of the south" or "son of the right hand" going back into the Tanakh (called the Hebrew Bible by Christian scholars), a name of one of the sons of Jacob. His name, "Ben," is to create a rhyming effect between his first name and the number Ten. Also, his surname, "Tennyson," is a reference to 'Ten' of Ben 10.

His middle name, Kirby, was named as reference to comic book artist [[wikipedia:Jack Kirby|Jack Kirby]].{{Refn|http://archive.is/klM3B|group = DJW}}

